The woman looks at me.
"And your phone number?" she asks.
I nod.
"Yes," I say.
"I have a Danish number now."
I got it from the shop today.
It is on a small card.
I read the numbers slowly.
"It is twelve..."
"...thirty-four..."
"...fifty-six..."
"...seventy-eight."
The woman writes my number down.
It is good to have a Danish phone number.
